I couldn't migrate `order-service`: permission to write was denied for all three files, so nothing in the repo has changed. Once you grant write access I'll apply the change and run `node --test tests/order-service.test.js`. I haven't run the tests yet.

**What I'd change:**

`src/services/order-service.js`: drop the direct `query` import and call `OrderRepository` instead. Both functions now return promises.
```js
import { OrderRepository } from '../repositories/order-repository.js';

const orders = new OrderRepository();

export function listOrdersForUser(userId) {
  return orders.findByUser(userId);
}

export async function totalPaidCents() {
  const rows = await orders.findPaid();
  return rows.reduce((sum, o) => sum + o.total_cents, 0);
}
```
The repository uses the same filters as the old code (`user_id`/`deleted_at`, and `status === 'paid'`/`deleted_at`), so the results stay the same.

`tests/order-service.test.js`: make both tests `async`, `await` the functions, and keep the same assertions.

`src/api/routes.js`: this file is outside the module, but it calls these two functions with callbacks, so switching them to promises would break `/users/:id/orders` and `/reports/paid-total`. I'd change those two handlers so they still pass results to the callback:
```js
handler: (req, cb) => listOrdersForUser(Number(req.params.id)).then((rows) => cb(null, rows), cb)
handler: (req, cb) => totalPaidCents().then((total) => cb(null, total), cb)
```
The other routes stay as they are.

